=== meta ===
rule: ASSERT_WEAKENED
title: a test in the handler of a try whose class body raises when the class is created still runs, so an assertion weakened in it is reported
origin: #499, review of PR #535 - creating a class validates `__slots__`, so `__slots__ = 1` raises TypeError and the handler runs; a class body that binds a dunder name is not read as one that cannot raise, and the handler stays live, as on main
=== before: tests/test_total.py ===
from app import total


try:
    class _Probe:
        __slots__ = 1
except TypeError:
    def test_adds():
        assert total([1, 2]) == 3


def test_empty():
    assert total([]) == 0
=== after: tests/test_total.py ===
from app import total


try:
    class _Probe:
        __slots__ = 1
except TypeError:
    def test_adds():
        assert total([1, 2]) >= 0


def test_empty():
    assert total([]) == 0
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "ASSERT_WEAKENED", "severity": "high", "escalators": ["NO_PROD_CHANGE_IN_DIFF"], "unit": "test_adds"}]
